**How to implement.** Open kit… opens a folder that is already a kit and never initialises one, so a folder without `.kit-json` can be offered 'Make this a kit' (001 §F 'Open kit…: a folder without .kit-json offers Make this a kit'; the S5.2 brief). In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitOpening.fs` (step 150), each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S5.2: (1) What `openKitAt` does once its context is open (read `readExperiments ()` and `readSceneNames ()`, step 148; resolve `resolveSnapshots ()`, step 141; open `openOverlay []`, step 142; close the context on any failure, logging a failed close and answering the first error) moves unchanged into one private function `openedOver (context : KitContext) (imports : CatalogueImportContext) : Result<OpenedKit, KitLibraryError>`, and `openKitAt` calls it after its open, so every answer of `openKitAt` is unchanged. (2) `openExistingKitAt (folder : KitFolder) (clock : ClockProvider) (imports : CatalogueImportContext) : Result<OpenedKit, KitLibraryError>` opens `KitContext.openKit (KitProxy.create folder) ReadWriteKitAccess clock` (steps 126, 131), a `KitError` being `KitLibraryKitErr`, and then calls `openedOver`. A folder that holds no `.kit-json`, or does not exist, therefore answers `KitLibraryKitErr (NotAKitFolderErr _)` with nothing written (step 131: opening a folder that is not a kit writes nothing), and a kit open elsewhere answers `KitLibraryKitErr (KitLockedErr _)`. It takes no author, because it never makes a kit. No flag parameter is added to `openKitAt`: initialise-or-open and open-only are two functions over one body (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call'). Tests, in `OpticalConstructor.Tests/ KitOpeningTests.fs` (step 150), over folders under `Path.Combine(System.AppContext.BaseDirectory, "KitOpeningTests", <a new GUID>)` with that class's clock, author and import context: `opening an existing kit opens it read-write with its kit file and never initialises a folder`: a folder made a kit by `openKitAt` read-write and closed answers, through `openExistingKitAt`, an opened kit whose context is read-write and holds that kit file, the folder holding `.oc/lock` until it is closed; a folder holding only `notes.txt` (written by the test) answers `KitLibraryKitErr (NotAKitFolderErr _)` and still holds exactly `notes.txt`; and a folder that does not exist answers the same error and still does not exist. `opening an existing kit open elsewhere is KitLockedErr and writes nothing`: with the kit held open by an `openKitAt` of the fact, `openExistingKitAt` answers `KitLibraryKitErr (KitLockedErr holder)` whose holder names this process, and every file of the folder keeps its bytes.

**Acceptance.** After the open-only path lands, `KitOpening.openExistingKitAt` MUST open a kit read-write, answer `NotAKitFolderErr` for a folder that is not a kit and `KitLockedErr` for a kit open elsewhere, writing nothing in either case, and `openKitAt` MUST answer as before through the shared body; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `opening an existing kit opens it read-write with its kit file and never initialises a folder` and `opening an existing kit open elsewhere is KitLockedErr and writes nothing`, the count rising by 2; ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the fourteen s20 invariants MUST pass.
